WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:12.470
I don't normally do these kind of speeches
but this feels like a big moment.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:18.184
I know it's not easy being banished
from MI5 to my department,

00:00:19.144 --> 00:00:20.770
but that's on you.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:24.065
Only screw-ups get sent to Slough House,

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:25.233
and I got to be honest

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.696
working with you has been the lowest point
in a disappointing career.

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:32.365
Right.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:36.119
What are you looking for?

00:00:36.119 --> 00:00:38.580
The remnants of a once promising career.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.293
Slough House is like prison.
You’re not supposed to ask what you’re in for.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.628
I actually want to be useful.

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:47.589
I could not be more bored if I tried.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.883
You probably know how many
people have made it back

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:52.844
from Slough House to upstairs
here at Regent's Park.

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:56.848
Bringing you up to speed is like
trying to explain Norway to a dog.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:57.640
None.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.143
Come check this out.

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:01.603
Hostage.

00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:02.896
He's being held here.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.356
There is something finally happening.

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:07.901
What does it got to do with you? 

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:11.029
Whatever's going on will be
handled by the real agents.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:17.076
I get it. We're just slow horses.

00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:18.995
I’ve got one lead. I have to follow it.

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:22.999
You're going to help me.

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:24.209
No, I'm not.

00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:26.836
Like it or not, Slough House
is part of this now.

00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:28.838
What do you think you're playing at?

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:32.634
I didn't mean to kill him.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.303
Of course you didn't.
If you meant to kill him he'd still be alive.

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:38.973
You put lives in danger.

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:40.767
This is off the books!

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.937
I am directing personnel,

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.772
Yours or anybody else's.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.818
She's covering her tracks.

00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:53.363
It's the covering of the tracks
that always gets you in the end.

00:01:56.741 --> 00:01:58.576
You really care about them don't you?

00:01:58.576 --> 00:02:01.871
No. I think they’re a bunch of absolute losers.

00:02:03.164 --> 00:02:04.958
But they’re my losers.

